cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RedGap in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "RedGap"
abstract: >-
  RedGap is an automated, MITRE ATT&CK-mapped offense/detection coverage harness.
  It runs benign ATT&CK techniques against a disposable local lab, captures real
  telemetry with an independent collector, and deterministically decides - from logs
  and Sigma rules, with no AI in the verdict - whether each technique was detected or
  is a gap. It also scores your own Sigma rules and surfaces SILENT rules: rules tagged
  to a technique that pass their own unit test yet never fire on real telemetry.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "befnoz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/befnoz/redgap"
url: "https://befnoz.github.io/redgap/"
